tensor/tensor.ml: random_seeds_created (ref) -- accounted: every write noted or at a boundary; captured by capture_globals
tensor/tensor.ml: open_nodes (ref) -- exempt: a record of what the open work allocated: an entry left by a failure that did not taint is a node nobody holds, which a later rewind discards and a closure forgets; captured by capture_globals
tensor/tensor.ml: handouts.fwd_out (mutable field) -- accounted; kept by rewinds: a record of code given to callers, which no rewind takes back
tensor/tensor.ml: handouts.bprop_out (mutable field) -- accounted; kept by rewinds: a record of code given to callers, which no rewind takes back
tensor/tensor.ml: last_closure (ref) -- accounted; kept by rewinds: the last closure's checkpoint: a closure records it, and no rewind restores an older one
tensor/tensor.ml: discarded_nodes (Hashtbl) -- accounted; kept by rewinds: a registry of what rewinds discarded: rewinds extend it, never restore it
tensor/tensor.ml: discarded_window_nodes_table (ref) -- accounted; kept by rewinds: a registry of the nodes id-neutral windows discarded, held weakly: windows extend it, never restore it
tensor/tensor.ml: id_neutral_depth (ref) -- exempt: the nesting of id-neutral windows, restored by their own finally
tensor/tensor.ml: window_discarded_nodes (ref) -- exempt: scratch of the current id-neutral window, emptied when it ends
tensor/tensor.ml: default_value_prec (ref) -- exempt: user configuration read when a tensor is built, not inference state
tensor/tensor.ml: default_grad_prec (ref) -- exempt: user configuration read when a tensor is built, not inference state
tensor/tensor.ml: max_sublabel_length (ref) -- exempt: user configuration of label printing, not inference state
tensor/tensor.ml: param_postprocess (ref) -- exempt: a user-installed hook applied to new parameters, not inference state
tensor/tensor.ml: applications (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: reserved_next_id (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: id_neutral_sabotaged (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: observers (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: generation (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: mode_override (unread state) -- exempt
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary note_external_handout -- a closed-world act: records that work left the session, so a rewind does not resurrect it; not open inference state
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary record_checkpoint -- the closure's record: run at the commit of a successful finish_inference, and to re-anchor after a rewind or a session reset
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary discarded_window_nodes -- the weak registry's creation on first use: an empty registry, which no rewind restores
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary finally -- a scoped restore: puts back the roots saved at entry, on return and on a raise alike
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary with_saved_random_seed -- a scoped restore: puts back the seed saved at entry, on return and on a raise alike
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary end_id_neutral_window -- the end of an id-neutral window: it compacts what the window's rewinds discarded, which no rewind restores
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary restore_checkpoint -- the rewind: it restores the checkpoint and clears the taint
tensor/tensor.ml: boundary unsafe_reinitialize -- the session reset: it discards all state and clears the taint
